# The same policy as ../input.lg with its declarations reordered: the human
# before the actor, the reservation before the gates it keys on, the gates
# swapped, and both groups of cords reversed. A reordering yields the same
# per-gate verdicts and master decisions (SPEC §7.5, rule 2); each activation
# reaches one gate, so there is no topological tie and the log trace is also
# the same as against ../input.lg (rule 3).
human  alice  role legal
reserve automated_decision by legal when risk >= high
actor  bot7
gate   decide  risk high   grant bot7
gate   draft   risk low    grant bot7
cord decide -> master
cord draft  -> master
cord bot7   -> decide
cord bot7   -> draft
